From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:05:26 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2-ctrls: reject invalid AV1 context tiles
 and VP9 tile rows

Complete AV1 tile validation with the context-update tile index bound,
which also rejects empty tile grids. Keep the existing descriptor-count
limit. Reject VP9 tile_rows_log2 above two before drivers use it in shifts
or tile loops.

These checks match the public AVD v3 series by Sofus Forstreuter.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-media/20261020-avd-v3-4-85cbaa2125d8@icloud.com/
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-media/20261020-avd-v3-5-85cbaa2125d8@icloud.com/
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
index 648b88c868..0db4d34f1f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-ctrls-core.c
@@ -629,9 +629,9 @@ validate_vp9_frame(struct v4l2_ctrl_vp9_frame *frame)
 
 	/*
 	 * According to the spec, tile_cols_log2 shall be less than or equal
-	 * to 6.
+	 * to 6, and tile_rows_log2 shall be less than or equal to 2.
 	 */
-	if (frame->tile_cols_log2 > 6)
+	if (frame->tile_cols_log2 > 6 || frame->tile_rows_log2 > 2)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (frame->reference_mode > V4L2_VP9_REFERENCE_MODE_SELECT)
@@ -804,7 +804,8 @@ static int validate_av1_tile_info(struct v4l2_av1_tile_info *t)
 	    t->tile_rows > V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_ROWS)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if ((u32)t->tile_cols * t->tile_rows > V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_COUNT)
+	if ((u32)t->tile_cols * t->tile_rows > V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_COUNT ||
+	    t->context_update_tile_id >= (u32)t->tile_cols * t->tile_rows)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	return 0;
-- 
